.TH elfshaker 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" 
.SH NAME
elfshaker
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker\fR [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enables verbose description of the execution process.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Set the path to the elfshaker repository.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
elfshaker\-extract(1)
Can be used to extract a snapshot.
.TP
elfshaker\-store(1)
Stores the current state of the repository in a snapshot. The snapshots created in this way can later be packed in a .pack file using the pack command.
.TP
elfshaker\-list(1)
Prints the list of snapshots available in the repository.
.TP
elfshaker\-list\-packs(1)
Prints the list of packs available in the repository.
.TP
elfshaker\-list\-files(1)
Prints the list of files available in the snapshot.
.TP
elfshaker\-pack(1)
Packs the given snapshots into a pack file.
.TP
elfshaker\-show(1)
Shows the contents of the files in the snapshot.
.TP
elfshaker\-find(1)
Searches the repository index.
.TP
elfshaker\-gc(1)
Cleanup redundant snapshots and unreferenced objects. This frees up disk space after creating a pack.
.TP
elfshaker\-update(1)
Updates the remote indexes.
.TP
elfshaker\-clone(1)
Clones a remote repository into a new directory
.TP
elfshaker\-explode(1)
Explodes a pack into loose objects
.SH VERSION
v1.0.0\-rc1
